> <<
> 
> That means that if I call a function with a non-initialised double it won't be
> detected. But it should.

IMO, you mis-interpret the docu: 
Sure, "splint" will not detect that the current function was called 
with a non-initialised double, 
but it will (hopefully) detect that the current function _is_calling_ 
some other with a non-initialised double, and that is the point of 
error which needs to be corrected.


