Hi,

when compiling the attached program I hit a bug in the
compiler as shipped in Redhat 7.1 (gcc-2.96-87).

Can someone with a Redhat 7.2 installation compile
it and send me the assembler output? If the bug
is also in 7.2 I will try to submit a bug report.

You need to compile it towards a kernel tree that
is configured for SMP and EV6 CPUs.
With ommiting the -mcpu=ev6 compiler option the
problem disappears.

What happens:
when calling an inline function (bogus_inline in the
example) the inlining of the function fails.
At the begin of the function the argument calculated
inside the inline gets computed half through and
stored on the stack [ 80($30) ]. The first instance
of the inline functions used the half computed argument
from the stack while the second instance computes all over
correctly and used the correct result.
Details are in the comments in the C code.

Regards, Martin

