Hi everybody,

My Alpha had been sitting on the shelf for a couple years before I finally 
brought it out to play with it again.  It's a 164LX.  When I last was 
tinkering with it, I installed an old version of SuSE on it.  
Unfortunately, while doing so I also set the SRM's auto_boot to 
automagically load MILO.  I really don't want to do this any more, I just 
want the SRM prompt.

I've tried hooking the reset switch up to the halt jumper on the MB 
(that's J22), but that didn't work -- it still acted like a reset switch.  
I tried updating the firmware, which I think worked, and I've tried 
hitting control-c and control-p while it's booting.  None of this helped 
-- it still heads right into MILO.

Does anybody have any advice for preventing this behavior?  I just want 
that beautiful little SRM prompt so I can get control of my Alpha back!

Thanks!

-- 
