On Sun, Jul 07, 2002 at 02:12:35PM -0700, Erik Arneson wrote:
> 
> It looks like it must be loading MILO directly.  I don't see any SRM stuff 
> or any AlphaBIOS stuff.  After the video card initialization, it prints 
> out four or five lines starting with "dev_config:fixing up latency", then 
> drops straight to a MILO prompt.
> 
> In between the two, a screen flashes very quickly, but I can't catch what 
> it says.

If you unhook all the disks/floppies, and it *still* boots into MILO,
then you probably FLASHed MILO the last time you were using it.

Go back over the MILO FLASHing docs, and see if they give any way to
re-FLASH SRM. Or you may be forced to use the Debug Monitor technique
to re-establish SRM in the FLASH.

 --Jay++

