On Mon, 8 Jul 2002, Erik Arneson wrote:

> Thanks to Michal Jaegermann, I was able to fix my 164LX.  He figured out 
> that I must have been running ARC, and that for some reason long ago I 
> flashed the nvram with a MILO image or something stupid like that.  ;)  
> Anyhow, I fixed it by loading a new AlphaBIOS update, then switching over 
> to SRM.  I'm now running the SRM console, and it's working great.
> 
> After finishing this, I went about trying to install RedHat 7.1 via ftp.  
> It went very smoothly, and I was impressed.  However, I ran into one 
> problem.  I chose automatic partitioning, and it chose the Linux-style 
> partitions over BSD-style disklabels.  I suspect this might be because the 
> disks were already partitioned.  Could I fix this by wiping the SCSI disk 
> partitions before doing the install?

Yes, usually a 'dd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/sda count=4' will take care of 
that problem (I think that's right, but it has been a while).
 
> Has anybody seen this problem before?  I don't mind reinstalling, because 
> it looks like I'll have to repartition my drives anyhow.  I'm just 
> wondering if there are any other partitioning caveats I should know about 
> before I begin anew.

Yes the RH installer will only use BSD disk labels if the disk is already 
labeled that way or has no label.

FYI, 7.2 for alpha has been released as well, you may want to take a look 
at that.

