alvin <alvin@iplink.net> writes:

> I believe there to be a bug in calloc. I have a couple of programs one
> of which is a small disk space check program from netsaint. I have not
> been yet able to create a small program that will recreate the error but
> I keep getting a segfault in the chunck_alloc code.
> 
> I have run up dmalloc to see if there is a problem with the actuall use
> of calloc and the problem then goes away. I have run dmalloc on another
> offending program and the problem that I have there also seems to go
> away.
> 
> Does anybody else know about this and possibly have a fix or am I going
> to be spending a few days whakcing my head against the malloc code.

It is is unlikely that this is a bug in malloc; malloc is very mature
code. More likely, it is a bug in your code that destroys malloc's
internal structures, the classical example being array overruns. We
cannot decide that though without a test case.

If you have an i386 with Linux, you might want to try valgrind, a
memory debugger which can catch such errors.

-- 
	Falk




