On Fri, Jul 12, 2002 at 01:36:53PM -0500, Mark Hansel wrote:
> ImageMagick causes X to loose the new window borders, to add the "feature"
> of beeping on screen switches (alt-Fx) and to beep on various mouse
> clicks. I was using display to make quick rescaling of some figures. It is
> reproducible and requires restarting X. Gimp is overkill
> 
> I don't know if this is related or independent. After restarting X and
> printing from mozilla, the X server froze. I could access the machine from
> another box.  "top" reported X sucking up most of the cycles. None of the
> processes running under X would die (kill -9 <pid) or killall -9 <process
> name>) and neither X nor gdm would go away.
> 
> I'm using gdm, XF86_SVGA (matrox millenium), sawfish.

You should be using the XFree86 4.1.0 stuff that's on 7.2, rather than
the older 3.3.6 release.

Unfortunately, the install defaults to the 3.3.6 SVGA server for
Millenniums; you should be able to switch over to 4.1.0 by simply
changing the link in /etc/X11 for X to point to
/usr/X11R6/bin/XFree86.

Good luck.

 --Jay++

