On Fri, Jul 12, 2002 at 07:21:48PM -0500, Mark Hansel wrote:
> 
> The server seems more stable. However, (after running display and doing
> the offending manipulations) some of the novel featurs are still present.  
> New windows pop up where -geometry says. No bop border, no ability to
> move. I can "grab" and edge or bottom corner and enlarge/contract, The
> "bell" feature remains when switching virtual desktops and on some
> keypresses (^D in an Xterm). It also seems to have trouble keeping track 
> of repeating keys -- this mail is on a remote machine --8 or 9 hops away 
> usually-- and I have to feed keystrokes one at a time.

What depth are you running at? If 24, make sure fbbpp is 32, ie:

	startx -- -depth 24 -fbbpp 32

Also, do the same things go bad if you run at depth 16? How about if
you add:

	Option "NoAccel"

to the Device Section?

Oh, and look at the man page for "kbdrate" for setting repeat rates and
such...

 --Jay++

