On Mon, Jul 15, 2002 at 09:30:39PM -0500, Earl Truss wrote:
>
> Sorry, forgot to mention that ... It has only 256MB.

OK, so it's not too much memory... ;-}

On the DAC960 card, there should be a couple of small square-ish
sockets, close together, one empty, the other with a chip (EPROM) in
it. On the chip should be a label with a few numbers, one of which is
the revision of the FW in the chip. I'm betting that yours is most
likely a 2.38 or 2.40 revision. The DAC960 Linux driver will only work
with FW revisions 2.73 or higher.

 --Jay++

