I'm getting a kernel paging request error that kills
a very large ab-initio calculation I'm trying to run
using gamess compiled with the Compaq fortran compiler.
The program itself complains that a child process has
been terminated before it stops.  The /var/log/messages file
lines related to crash time are listed below.
I presently have 4 Gb of swap space but I suspect that
it may not be enough.   I have been making more swap files
of 1400000 blocks of 1024 and have experimented with
making larger ones, but when I make a file of 5 million blocks
(dd if=/dev/zero of=SWAP5 bs=1024 count=5000000)
and run mkswap SWAP5 I get 
mkswap: error: swap area needs to be at least 80 kB
where ls -l SWAP5 reports 5120000000, so I think there
is a problem in mkswap (alpha swap spaces (files?) can be
128 GiB, right?)

So, is this just a swap space issue, so that I can
continue to jack up my swap areas, or is there some
other problem with kernel paging?

