On Thu, Jul 18, 2002 at 01:27:07PM +0530, Aneesh Kumar K.V wrote:
> hi, 

"Jeopardy posting" is a very nasty habit.

> 	Also is there  anybody working on the 0(1) scheduler and pre-emptive
> kernel patches for alpha.Are these patches already available for alpha ?

> 
> On Thu, 2002-07-18 at 13:20, Heid Oliver wrote:
> > Hi, 
> > 
> > Is there any activity re supporting 2.5 kernels on alpha? I cannot even
> > compile any recent release (I tried 2.5.19 to 2.5.26). Are there specific
> > patches not posted on linux-kernel list?

Yes, patches were posted on linux-kernel list although the latest one
for 2.5.24 IIRC.  Likely they can be adapted for 2.5.26 but I did not
try. Playing with development kernels without watching linux-kernel
pretty close and for a while may cause nasty surprises.

As for O(1) scheduler then 2.5 kernels are using it.  Also on this
list it was annouced at least twice that variants of 2.4 kernels with
such scheduler are available.  Current kernels from "ac" series for
2.4.19-... should compile on Alpha (remains to be checked) and use
such scheduler.  The same should be true for "aa".

  Michal




