Hi Michal,

Re. 2.4.19 aa and ac kernels: The following ones did definitely not compile
(I tried on all of: UP2000, XP1000 (ev6), PC164, all on RH 7.1 with latest
updates):
2.4.19-pre10-ac2
2.4.19-rc1-aa2
2.4.19-rc1-ac1
2.4.19-rc1-ac4
2.4.19-rc1-ac5
True, there was a patch for 2.5.24: I could apply it successfully, but it
did not help. Among other things, most of these and the 2.5 kernels complain
about a missing __down_read_trylock__ function (IIRC), which are not fixed
by any of the many patches I found so far.
I'd would really be happy to have a (any) 2.4.19 or 2.5 kernel with O(1)
scheduling and lolat patches..

	Oliver

	>Yes, patches were posted on linux-kernel list although the latest
one
	>for 2.5.24 IIRC.  Likely they can be adapted for 2.5.26 but I did
not
	>try. Playing with development kernels without watching linux-kernel
	>pretty close and for a while may cause nasty surprises.
	>
	>As for O(1) scheduler then 2.5 kernels are using it.  Also on this
	>list it was annouced at least twice that variants of 2.4 kernels
with
	>such scheduler are available.  Current kernels from "ac" series for
	>2.4.19-... should compile on Alpha (remains to be checked) and use
	>such scheduler.  The same should be true for "aa".
