The same as "top posting".  An artificial reversal of a natural
progression, if you posted something with an intention of an exchange of
ideas, which makes much harder any conversation on line.

Especially nice if somebody writes "Yes." or "No." and leaves below 300
lines of an original.  If not posting Jeopardy style they would have at
least to do some editing work to achive similar effect and chances are
that such effort would stop them or at least give some pause for
thinking.

Why the name?  Think for a moment where you would be able to find
lines like that:

What does this mean?
"Jeopardy posting" is a very nasty habit.

See? :-)

   Michal




