While looking around in my AlphaServer 2100, I've discovered a card I
cannot identify.  It's in one of the upper-most EISA slots.  It has no
internal cables or connections that I can remember seeing.  On the
bulkhead, it has a female D-connector with three rows of holes with a
total of 50 pins.  When I do "show dev" in SRM, it seems to show up as a
"DBI0201".  I can identify all the other devices as the NCR SCSI
controllers, the Mylex controller, video card and two network cards.  I
have looked at all the documentation I can find and searched for this on
the "Digital" web site but have not found anything.  I'm tempted to pull
it out and see what disappears, if anything.




