Hi Jay,

I have a 8MB Millenium II.  I do not have a daughter card.  My card has a
row of four RAM chips on the front.  And on the back there are four more in
exactly the same places as the ones on the front.  The model number on the
card is "MIL2P/8N".  lspci shows the same output as the other card.

I've been running a Radeon 7000 in a LX164 for a couple of months, but I
just swapped cards to see if I could reproduce the problem.  I'm running
a home compile XFree86 4.2 with some Redhat patches.  It was compiled
with -mcpu=ev56.  If I do not specify the amount of video ram in Xconfig,
the server detects 4M.  If I specify 8M, the server accepts it.
However, with 8M it get corrupted graphics shortly after starting the
server.  It seems to trigger really easily by pushing a window offscreen
(even a little) and dragging it back on.  If I set "noaccel" to "on", the
corruption stops and things move real  slow.  I also have "PCIretry" set to
"on".

HTH,
Alan

