I'm interested in this as well.  There is a binary only DivX codec for
i386 linux available from www.divx.com .  I wonder how well it runs
under emulation. ;)

The DivX people are actually pretty good about supporting non-windows
OS's (even though they are closed source) but I don't know if they can
be convinced to port DivX 5 codec to non-i386 archs.  They are in the
business to make money (in fact I purchased the DivX 5 bundle for
windows), and I really do not know if it would be profitable for them to
port the software.

**WARNING: UN-INFORMED OPINION FOLLOWS, PLEASE TAKE AT YOUR OWN RISK**
A side note, the DivX 5 commercial codec really does get great results
and extremely high compression.  I wouldn't mind paying for a 'developer
license' and signing an NDA *gasp* if we could get this ported.  Making
the code 64-bit clean would be beneficial to their company for the new
processors coming from Intel and AMD.

Ted

