"Ted Goodridge, Jr" <tedgoodridgejr@acm.org> writes:

> How optimized is ffmpeg for alpha? I'm just curious as to how  (I don't
> remember what they are called, they are like MMX, on crack) this was
> done because I'm extremely interested in looking at other apps and
> seeing if they can be optimized for the alpha.  I may be in way over my
> head, but worth a shot ;)

It is pretty optimized; I would be interested in any improvements,
though :) It also uses the MVI instruction extension if available;
unfortunately, it is not terribly helpful since it lacks subword
addition and especially subword multiplication (as much as I like the
Alpha design, MVI is a bit of an aberration...).

The main time sink is the IDCT; so if you want to help, give
simple_idct.c a try... it has to do lots of multiplies of 16-bit
shorts with constants. I've tried abusing the FP multiplier for this,
but it isn't really faster, since on ev5 moving data between integer
and FP registers is not possible directly... perhaps it'll work on
ev6.

-- 
	Falk




