Actually, it's the other way around in this case.

API made the CS20 and CPQ/HP made the DS20L based on it.

The only differences between them (besides the front cover) are the SRM
and the SCSI controller on the PCI riser card.

The CS20 uses an LSI Logic based U3W controller, while the CPQ/HP uses an 
Adaptec based U3W SCSI controller to be supported in Tru64.

Linux supports it just fine as long as you use a kernel that has the 
support for the apropriate SCSI controller.

I'm not sure on BSD on them though. The hardware is essentially DP264 / 
DS20 with a different onboard SCSI card, built in NICs and faster CPUs / 
Cache. It *should* run assuming it supports the SCSI controller.


Kurt


