I don't think so, I have a Miata PWS433au having 64MB ECC SDRAM and it works fine with SuSE 7.2 Alpha Edition, XFree86 3.3.6 (4.x.x versions are RAM consuming monsters), IceWM, Koffice 1.1.1 etc... 
Au contraire, I think 64 bit architectures (or just the Alpha systems) use more efficiently the disponible physical RAM than 32 bit systems do (according to my personal experiences). I think it is true for the use of the swap partition also.
However I am looking for some RAM upgrade but the original RAM kits are quite expensive for my budget. The disponible amount of RAM is never enough....
 
On the other hand is there someone who made working SetiAtHome's Alpha/Linux client? 

VV




