Maurice Hilarius wrote:
> 
> With regards to your message at 01:39 AM 7/31/02, Danilo Godec. Where you
> stated:
> >While on the subject of memory and Alphas... I have one 164SX and ever
> >since I have a feeling, it NEEDs more RAM than her i386 buddies around
> >here.
> >
> >Is this correct? Does an Alpha require more RAM for (somewhat) equal
> >operation than a i386 based machine just due to the 64 bit architecture?
> 
> While this is not definitive, nor any kind of expert answer, I see that
> many binaries compiled for Alpha 64 bit are physically larger files than
> their x86 equivalents..

RISC processors will allways have code sizes larger than the x86. The
x86 code is variable length and is a CISC(Complex Instruction Set
Computer). 

the 64 bit alignment and int size will mean that the data size will tend
to be larger also. since the x86 has no real restrictions on alignment
although performance can be improved by the correct alignment. Also 32
bit ints take half the size.

